\f1\fs22 \'93They are totally possessed by Jesus, High Elvis.\'94 Kleo reluctantly admitted. \'93Chilo, Solo and I have been working non-stop for 7 days, but nothing seemed to penetrate the mindlessness of their faith. They cannot seem to ignore the false promise of life ever-lasting, the dishonest certainty of faith.\'94 Each Elvis held fast to their belief, in the face of irresistible logical argument thrown at them by the wise three.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93What next, great one.\'94 High Elvis wanted to hear better news, but was hopeful the next round of treatment may work.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I think we have no choice, but to adopt some ancient methods from antiquity.\'94 Kleo was deliberately vague, he did not want to use the word exorcism, because it would not be an entirely accurate description and would not be met with any enthusiasm. \'93Initially, I would suggest we try the new protocols on one Elvis only. If we make errors, it will only affect one Elvis and we can improve as we process them one at a time.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93They are not to be harmed deliberately. My cabinet colleagues and I are most adamant that no harm come to them.\'94 The High Elvis had mentioned his abhorrence to violence being visited upon his precious creed of clones far too many times for Kleo to forget. \'93I am placing my faith in you, great Sages.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Thank you, High Elvis.\'94 Kleo bowed his head slightly. \'93Solo and Chilo, we shall prepare ourselves to fight this insidious Jesus.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93This is a fight for the hearts and minds of all the Elvi, we cannot afford to lose.\'94 Solo followed Kleo out of the President\'92s Office and prepared himself to do battle with evil.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>* * *\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>A scratchy recording of \'91Great Balls of Fire\'92 was playing softly in the cell of Christian Elvis 1. His restraints had been removed, but he was not rhythmically gyrating to the music, there were no pelvic thrusts or fancy footwork. He was on his knees in the corner, hands clasped together and talking quietly to himself. He stood up and turned the three Sages and calmly sat on the single bed, the only piece of furniture in the room.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93For your safety and ours, we are going to restrain you now, Elvis.\'94 Kleo said softy, looking deeply into his mesmerising blue eyes as Solo and Chilo gently attached the manacled Elvis to the bed. He remained calm and did not resist.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Do you know what she did? Your confronting daughter?\'94 Elvis was looking directly at Kleo, as his eyes rolled back, exposing nothing but white. \'93Your daughter sucks lolly-pops in heaven.\'94 As he spoke Kleo heard more that one voice, perhaps a score of voices on top of one another, not in a demonic hash of mournful howls, but an angelic chorus.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Do not speak of her, Elvis. She has nothing to do with this.\'94 Kleo was clearly shocked, the painful memory of his daughter slicing through his heart, momentarily blind-siding him.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I am not Elvis. I am Jesus of Nazareth. Your daughter is here with me and she forgives you.\'94 His voices were now of higher pitch, but a monotone of serenity, his face beaming grace.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Your parlour tricks are no match for the power of the Dawkins. Tell me Elvis, do you speak the ancient biblical language?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Sanscrit? 
