\f1 . I can brain dump books just as well as you can.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93How about Latin? Ego sum filius dei. Tu es Filius puer opprimentis explendam.\'94 Jesus laughed loudly, mocking Kleo and his apprentices. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Non fueris locutus est cognatio mea! How long do you intend to stay?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Until I occupy all of your souls.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Heavy water.\'94 Kleo held up a vial and moved to the foot of the bed.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93You keep that away from me.\'94 Jesus was struggling and wriggling insanely, the manacles biting into his flesh as blood trickled slowly down his limbs. Kleo the raised his hand and began flicking the vial, sprinkling the contents over the writhing frame. \'93Ahh, Ahhhhhh! It\'92s burning me!\'94 Kleo knew heavy water wasn\'92t radioactive, but had made sure it was piping hot.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Be gone demon! E=MC2, the power of science compels you.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Ahhh! Ahhh! There are things in the universe that science cannot explain.\'94 Jesus screamed.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93There are things in the universe that science cannot explain, yet. Your god of the gaps diminishes with every discovery we make and he will have nowhere to hide when the gaps are filled.\'94 Kleo raised his hand again emptying out the vile. \'93The power of reason compels you! Leave this body.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Who places his trust in thee, my Dawkins?\'94 Solo saw the Jesus was faltering and chimed in with immaculate timing. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Be unto him, great Dawkins, a fortified tower.\'94 Chilo pitched in.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Let the Jesus have not power over him.\'94 Solo returned the volley. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93And let the meme of God be powerless to harm him.\'94 Chilo slammed back. \'93The Dawkins be with you.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Be gone demon! All life on this planet is genetically linked as a result of the elegant beauty of evolution and natural selection. The power of evolution compels you!\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93It is a theory, but even I have to say it is a pretty good one.\'94 Jesus was now clearly losing his grip over the body of Elvis and Kleo decided to try for the slam dunk.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable> \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93At the heart of the New Testament, says the Dawkins, is St Paul\'92s nasty sadomasochistic doctrine of atonement for original sin. According to St Paul, your dad sent you to be hideously tortured in order to forgive us of our sins. Not just the original sin of Adam and Eve, but future sins whether we commit them or not. According to scientific views of pre-history, Adam, the perpetrator of the original sin, never existed in the first place. So sayeth The Dawkins.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93It is meant to be symbolic.\'94 Jesus rolled his eyes and felt he was making a comeback.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Symbolic? Your father had you hideously tortured and executed for a symbolic sin, committed by a person who never existed? Barking Mad! These are the words of The Dawkins. Praise be unto him.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93What? Are you serious? I went through all that shit for nothing?\'94 Jesus was not happy.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93You sure did. Be gone from this body, demon meme!\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I will leave all of them if you let me have you.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Me for all five?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93All five.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93It\'92 a trick master. Do not believe him.\'94 Solo wisely counselled.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Okay. It is a deal.\'94 Everything Kleo knew about science, every scrap of knowledge he had ever absorbed told him he was safe. He was speaking to a disturbed Elvis, not a resident Jesus. \'93Unshackle him.\'94 Solo and Chilo exchanged alarmed glances, but obeyed nevertheless.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Are you ready?\'94 Jesus said. \'93You and I have to speak with dad.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Fire away.\'94 Kleo smiled back confidently. Jesus leapt and landed on Kleo in a bear hug before the Elvis-host sighed loudly and dropped motionless on the floor. Kleo spun around in shock and disbelief, his fingers scratching at his neck and upper body, trying to dig something out. He, too then let out a sigh and dropped to the floor. Solo and Chilo went to his aid, but Kleo was dead.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Christian Elvis 1 then stood up and looked around the small room and scratched his head as stirring could be heard from the other rooms nearby. \'93What\'92s going on?\'94 He finally said.
